-- The triggers: disabling, changing when they fire, or dropping them is
-- refused, whatever the spelling.
ALTER TABLE repack_safe.rewrites
    DISABLE TRIGGER rewrites_protected;
ERROR:  cannot change when trigger rewrites_protected on table repack_safe.rewrites fires
DETAIL:  The record table's triggers refuse every change to the records but the extension's own, and must fire ALWAYS.
ALTER TABLE repack_safe.rewrites DISABLE TRIGGER ALL;
ERROR:  cannot change when trigger rewrites_protected on table repack_safe.rewrites fires
DETAIL:  The record table's triggers refuse every change to the records but the extension's own, and must fire ALWAYS.
ALTER TABLE repack_safe.rewrites DISABLE TRIGGER USER;
ERROR:  cannot change when trigger rewrites_protected on table repack_safe.rewrites fires
DETAIL:  The record table's triggers refuse every change to the records but the extension's own, and must fire ALWAYS.
ALTER TABLE repack_safe.rewrites
    ENABLE TRIGGER rewrites_protected;
ERROR:  cannot change when trigger rewrites_protected on table repack_safe.rewrites fires
DETAIL:  The record table's triggers refuse every change to the records but the extension's own, and must fire ALWAYS.
ALTER TABLE repack_safe.rewrites
    ENABLE REPLICA TRIGGER rewrites_protected;
ERROR:  cannot change when trigger rewrites_protected on table repack_safe.rewrites fires
DETAIL:  The record table's triggers refuse every change to the records but the extension's own, and must fire ALWAYS.
ALTER TABLE repack_safe.rewrites
    DISABLE TRIGGER rewrites_writer_only;
ERROR:  cannot change when trigger rewrites_writer_only on table repack_safe.rewrites fires
DETAIL:  The record table's triggers refuse every change to the records but the extension's own, and must fire ALWAYS.
ALTER TABLE repack_safe.rewrites
    ENABLE TRIGGER rewrites_writer_only;
ERROR:  cannot change when trigger rewrites_writer_only on table repack_safe.rewrites fires
DETAIL:  The record table's triggers refuse every change to the records but the extension's own, and must fire ALWAYS.
ALTER TABLE repack_safe.rewrites
    ENABLE REPLICA TRIGGER rewrites_writer_only;
ERROR:  cannot change when trigger rewrites_writer_only on table repack_safe.rewrites fires
DETAIL:  The record table's triggers refuse every change to the records but the extension's own, and must fire ALWAYS.
DROP TRIGGER rewrites_protected ON repack_safe.rewrites;
ERROR:  cannot drop the pg_repack_safe extension, its record table or its triggers while the record table holds records
DETAIL:  The statement would drop trigger rewrites_protected on table repack_safe.rewrites. A snapshot taken before a recorded REPACK (CONCURRENTLY), on this server or on any standby, would then read the rewritten table as empty.
HINT:  Delete the records with repack_safe.prune_records() and run VACUUM on the record table until it is empty (see the README, "Removing the extension"). A superuser can set pg_repack_safe.allow_unprotected_removal instead.
DROP TRIGGER rewrites_writer_only ON repack_safe.rewrites;
ERROR:  cannot drop the pg_repack_safe extension, its record table or its triggers while the record table holds records
DETAIL:  The statement would drop trigger rewrites_writer_only on table repack_safe.rewrites. A snapshot taken before a recorded REPACK (CONCURRENTLY), on this server or on any standby, would then read the rewritten table as empty.
HINT:  Delete the records with repack_safe.prune_records() and run VACUUM on the record table until it is empty (see the README, "Removing the extension"). A superuser can set pg_repack_safe.allow_unprotected_removal instead.
-- Dropping a trigger function with CASCADE would drop its trigger: refused.
-- (PostgreSQL itself refuses to drop a member of the extension, so the
-- function is detached first.)
ALTER EXTENSION pg_repack_safe DROP FUNCTION repack_safe.records_protected();
DROP FUNCTION repack_safe.records_protected();
ERROR:  cannot drop function repack_safe.records_protected() because other objects depend on it
DETAIL:  trigger rewrites_protected on table repack_safe.rewrites depends on function repack_safe.records_protected()
HINT:  Use DROP ... CASCADE to drop the dependent objects too.
