HINT:  Delete the records with repack_safe.prune_records() and run VACUUM on the record table until it is empty (see the README, "Removing the extension"). A superuser can set pg_repack_safe.allow_unprotected_removal instead.
ALTER EXTENSION pg_repack_safe ADD FUNCTION repack_safe.records_protected();
ALTER EXTENSION pg_repack_safe DROP FUNCTION repack_safe.records_writer_only();
DROP FUNCTION repack_safe.records_writer_only() CASCADE;
NOTICE:  drop cascades to trigger rewrites_writer_only on table repack_safe.rewrites
ERROR:  cannot drop the pg_repack_safe extension, its record table or its triggers while the record table holds records
DETAIL:  The statement would drop trigger rewrites_writer_only on table repack_safe.rewrites. A snapshot taken before a recorded REPACK (CONCURRENTLY), on this server or on any standby, would then read the rewritten table as empty.
HINT:  Delete the records with repack_safe.prune_records() and run VACUUM on the record table until it is empty (see the README, "Removing the extension"). A superuser can set pg_repack_safe.allow_unprotected_removal instead.
