DETAIL:  The statement would drop trigger rewrites_protected on table repack_safe.rewrites. A snapshot taken before a recorded REPACK (CONCURRENTLY), on this server or on any standby, would then read the rewritten table as empty.
HINT:  Delete the records with repack_safe.prune_records() and run VACUUM on the record table until it is empty (see the README, "Removing the extension"). A superuser can set pg_repack_safe.allow_unprotected_removal instead.
SELECT count(*) AS triggers FROM pg_trigger
WHERE tgrelid = 'repack_safe.rewrites'::regclass;
